    {
      "id": "413d5649-1d19-43bb-aeb2-e8e734018a23",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "## **Linked List**",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "413d5649-1d19-43bb-aeb2-e8e734018a23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e7501709-821b-4a85-9427-54a4c5dbb626",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 1.Linked List Creation",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "e7501709-821b-4a85-9427-54a4c5dbb626"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e1bdff62-1b58-4c2c-a473-25b4e55c4386",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "public class Node<T> {\r\n\r\n    public T data;\r\n    public Node<T> next;\r\n\r\n    public Node(T data){\r\n        this.data = data;\r\n        this.next = null;\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n\r\n// It contain data variable which will store the data of current node\r\n// Other is next variable which is another node object that will store next node for us\r\n// Then is the constructor which takes data from the user and set next node to null",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "e1bdff62-1b58-4c2c-a473-25b4e55c4386",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 2,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 2,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "id": "0d6224fb-c943-43d9-9579-d6e1303526ed",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 2. To Take Input From The User And Print The Taken Value",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "0d6224fb-c943-43d9-9579-d6e1303526ed"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d2eda5c1-da97-48a5-9bca-54c12aa368b3",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "// To take input from the user\r\npublic Node<Integer> takeInput(){\r\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\r\n        int data = sc.nextInt();\r\n\r\n        if(data == -1){\r\n            return null;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        Node<Integer> head = null;\r\n        Node<Integer> tail = null;\r\n\r\n        while(data != -1){\r\n\r\n            Node<Integer> currentNode = new Node<>(data);\r\n            if(head == null){\r\n                head = currentNode;\r\n                tail = currentNode;\r\n            }else{\r\n                tail.next = currentNode;\r\n                tail = currentNode;\r\n            }\r\n\r\n            data = sc.nextInt();\r\n        }\r\n        return head;\r\n    }\r\n   \r\n    // To print the nodes\r\n    // You can use temp to preserve the head node , so u can use it later or return it and use temp to traverse the linked likst\r\n    // temp can also be named as tail(generally people use tail in linked list as convention)\r\n    public void print(Node<Integer> head){\r\n\r\n        Node<Integer> temp = head;\r\n        while(temp != null){\r\n\r\n            System.out.print(temp.data + \" \");;\r\n            temp = temp.next;\r\n        }\r\n        System.out.println();\r\n\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    // To use takeInput() and print() method\r\n    Node<Integer> head = takeInput();\r\n    print(head);",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java",
        "id": "d2eda5c1-da97-48a5-9bca-54c12aa368b3",
        "executionSummary": {
          "executionOrder": 4,
          "success": true
        }
      },
      "execution_count": 4,
      "outputs": [
        {
          "output_type": "execute_result",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": "1 2 3 4 5 \r\n"
          },
          "metadata": {},
          "execution_count": 4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "27cc5978-dcc8-4788-b332-658b42e88eb9",
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": "### 3. To get the size of Linked List",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "markdown",
        "id": "27cc5978-dcc8-4788-b332-658b42e88eb9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c27c088d-4d72-4788-9587-3fc2840175bd",
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": "\r\npublic int getLength(Node<Integer> head){\r\n        Node<Integer> temp = head;\r\n        int count = 0;\r\n\r\n        while(temp != null){\r\n            count++;\r\n            temp = temp.next;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        return count;\r\n    }",
      "metadata": {
        "language": "java"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    }
  ]
}